<applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUKAWA, NOZOMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ODAGAWA, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAKIMA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ADACHI HIDEAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAMOTO MASAYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUKAWA NOZOMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ODAGAWA AKIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAKIMA HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ADACHI, HIDEAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAMOTO, MASAYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUKAWA, NOZOMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ODAGAWA, AKIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAKIMA, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A magnetoresistant device comprises a high-resistance layer (13) and first and second magnetic layers (12, 14) sandwiching the high-resistance layer (13). The high-resistance layer (13) is a barrier for allowing a tunnel current to flow between the first and second magnetic layer (12, 14) and contains at least on element LONC selected from among oxygen, nitrogen, and carbon. At least one layer (A) selected from among the first and second magnetic layers (12, 14) contains at least on metal element M selected from among Fe, Ni, and Co and an element RCP different from the metal element M. The element RCP is easily bonded to the element LONC in terms of energy compared to the metal element M. Thus, a novel magnetoresistant device having a low junction resistance and a high MR.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif magnétorésistant comprenant une couche haute résistance (13) et des première et second couches magnétiques (12, 14) de part et d'autre de la couche haute résistance (13) qui, en qualité de barrière, permet la circulation du courant en tunnel entre les couches (12, 14) et contient au moins un élément Lonc sélectionné dans un oxygène, un azote et un carbone. Au moins une couche (A) sélectionnée dans les deux couches magnétiques (12, 14) renferme au moins un élément métallique M sélectionné dans Fe, Ni et Co et un élément Rcp différent de l'élément métallique M. L'élément Rcp est facilement lié à l'élément Lonc en termes d'énergies en comparaison avec l'élément métallique M. Ainsi, on obtient un nouveau dispositif magnétorésistant ayant une faible résistance à la soudure et une forte résonance magnétique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>